# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-13, R-4, RC-6). L §5.14.2 Takes in the first batch: "A cycle among them (two places
# sweeping into each other in one batch, each arrival keeping labels) breaks where it can: each take is tried with the
# cycle's arrivals as parts of unknown labels, and a take whose outcome is the same under every reading of them ... is
# decided, which breaks the cycle. Otherwise a cycle that holds a plan is refused (RUN-CYCLE, naming the movements) ...
# A cycle of observed rows only is an unknown fact ...: the takes it reaches are undecided, each place holds a hole part
# with its total known (§8.1)".
# Owned places whose arrival rule keeps the owners by the leg read (rule keep: m.cash.amount of p / m.cash.amount):
# observed rows r1 and r2 between konto (ania's 100.00) and konto2 (tomek's 50.00) in one batch read each other's takes;
# each place holds a hole part with its total known (90.00, 60.00; scratch/exp6.py). L §8.1: a hole part keeps "the
# questions of what made it", so a share that is a HOLE-PART hole gives the hole part its own questions.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1
kind keeps: transfers
input bank: observed
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place konto2: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
input t1_day: date
input t1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
  rule keep beats base, t = m.cash.amount of p / m.cash.amount when m in keeps
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
move t1: tomeks
  on t1_day
  leg cash from world to konto2 amount t1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-01), bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of tomek, bal(konto2, 2026-03-01), bal(konto2, 2026-03-01) of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  t1_day = 2026-02-02
  t1_amt = 50.00 PLN
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-01, kind: keeps, leg cash from konto to konto2 amount 30.00 PLN) "r1"
  bank[r2] = (on: 2026-03-01, kind: keeps, leg cash from konto2 to konto amount 20.00 PLN) "r2"
=== expect
q: (90.00 PLN, ?"konto: 90.00 PLN may be ania's: which of bank[r1], bank[r2] went first on 2026-03-01?" (konto), ?"konto: 90.00 PLN may be tomek's: which of bank[r1], bank[r2] went first on 2026-03-01?" (konto), 60.00 PLN, ?"konto2: 60.00 PLN may be tomek's: which of bank[r1], bank[r2] went first on 2026-03-01?" (konto2))
  unfulfilled: a1
  unfulfilled: t1
  cut 2026-10-01
